Local modifications on 2026-10-29:
Documentation, file metadata, and the release status message were adjusted.
The original scientific methods and bundled Outcome/ research results remain upstream work.

Subsequent local research extension on 2026-10-29:
evifork_bio/, research/, tests/ and research_results/ add competing graph hypotheses,
optional audit-based evidence reliability, predictive calibration, information-gain query
selection and grouped holdout evaluation. They reuse the upstream algebraic simulator.
These retrospective and synthetic evaluations do not establish prospective biological
discovery or an independently verified new mechanism.

Distribution naming update on 2026-10-29:
This derivative distribution is named EviFork-Bio (Evidence forks for biological
causal hypotheses). Its Python entry point is python -m evifork_bio. Branded paths,
scripts and agent commands were renamed, with references updated. The distribution
name does not transfer authorship of the upstream FLASH-P methods, code, images,
paper or data. Scientific artifacts and LICENSE retain their original bytes;
historical identifiers remain for provenance and format compatibility. See
NAMING_MIGRATION.json for the complete path and checksum mapping.
